{{also|Bruno}}

==Italian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|it}} {{term|brunus|brūnus|lang=la}} "brown, brunet" (whence also {{etyl|es|-}} {{term|bruno|lang=es}}, {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|brun|lang=fr}}), of {{etyl|gem|it}} origin, from {{etyl|frk|it}} *{{term||brūn|lang=frk}}, from {{proto|Germanic|brūnaz|brown|lang=it}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|bher-|shining, brown|lang=it}}. Akin to {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|brun|brūn|lang=goh}} "brown" ({{etyl|de|-}} {{term|braun|lang=de}} "brown"), {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|brun|brūn|lang=ang}} "brown". More at {{l|en|brown}}.

===Adjective===
{{it-adj|brun}}

# (dark) [[brown]]

====Derived terms====
* [[orso bruno]]

===Noun===
{{it-noun|brun|m|o|i|f=bruna|fpl=brune}}

# a dark-haired person

